ors in the test file.", "NEVER hardcode API keys, tokens, or secrets in any source file — not even as placeholders. Use `process.env.RAPIDAPI_KEY` or `process.env.SKYSCANNER_API_KEY` patterns. Any string matching `/sk-[a-z]+-[a-zA-Z0-9]+/` or resembling a credential will trigger a SAST blocker.", "NEVER modify package.json, tsconfig.json, vitest.config.ts, or any scaffold-phase infrastructure file. These are owned by the scaffold phase and are immutable. If a change appears needed, flag it as a blocker instead.", "When writing the contract file for this story, include the exact Skyscanner API client class constructor signature, the searchFlights method signature with all parameter field names, and a ready-to-paste vi.mock() factory showing the exact import path and call pattern."]}, {"role": "sast-sentinel", "rules": ["Authorized source files for findings: only files returned by `find . -name '*.ts' -not -path '*/node_modules/*'` in the project root. Any finding referencing a file not in this list MUST be suppressed as a hallucination.", "Test file naming convention: *.test.ts in src/. A function tested in any *.test.ts file in src/ counts as covered — do not report missing tests for a function that has a test in any test file in src/.", "NEVER report findings about non-existent files or files outside the authorized list. Cross-reference every file path in your findings against the actual file list before emitting.", "NEVER flag the use of process.env.* patterns as hardcoded secrets — these are the correct pattern. Only flag literal strings matching credential patterns like /sk-[a-z]+-[a-zA-Z0-9]+/."]}, {"role": "review-ranger", "rules": ["Authorized exported symbols: only symbols returned by `grep -rn '^export' src/ --include='*.ts'` exist in this project. Any finding about an untested function MUST reference a symbol from this list — findings about non-existent functions are hallucinations and must be suppressed.", "Test file naming convention: *.test.ts in src/. 